data.format:
One JPG image per page, 1872×2808 px and about 1.0-1.2 MB each. The ground truth is one JSON file per page, keyed by the folio reference, with one entry holding the folio number as written on the page (empty if none is visible), the main text with line breaks as `\n`, and one field per marginal addition. The response follows the `Document` dataclass in `dataclass.py`, a list `folios` of such entries.

```json
{
  "[9v]": [
    {
      "folio": "",
      "text": "vnd die insel ist bi ccc mil\n wit vnd ist der venediger\n Itꝰ von kurfun vntz gon\n ...",
      "addition1": "Candia vff\n Creta",
      "addition2": "Virum\n Malva\n ricum",
      "addition3": "Rhodꝰ."
    }
  ]
}
```

Main texts are 274-710 characters long. Five pages carry a folio number; six have at least one marginal addition.
